<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42420" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρῐδ-αίνω</span></b> , impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠρίδαινον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Babr.
					68.3
				</span></i>
			 : 
				Ep.
			
			aor. I 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρίδηνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.89
				</span></i>
			 : —
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				5.105
			</span></i> : 
				Ep.
			
			aor. I inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρῑδήσασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.792
				</span></i>
			 (with vv. ll., dub.) ; elsewh. <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> uses only pres. : (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρίζω</span>):—<i>wrangle, quarrel,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετ᾽ ἀνδράσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					21.310
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὔτως γάρ ῥ᾽ ἐπέεσσ᾽ ἐριδαίνομεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.342
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῦν δὲ περὶ πτωχῶν ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					18.403
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ δὴ σφὼ ἕνεκα θνητῶν ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.574
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἵνεκα τῆς ἀρετῆς ἐ.</span>
			we <i>strive</i> (as for a prize) for her excellence, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.206
			</span></i> : c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὖρός τε Νότος τ᾽ ἐριδαίνετον
					ἀλλήλοιιν.. πελεμιζέμεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.765
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.89
			</span></i> ; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντία πάντων.. ἐριδαινέμεν οἶος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.79
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι</span> in a thing, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Dian.</u>
				262
			</span></i> ; of war, first in <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.986
			</span></i>, etc.:—
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποσσὶν ἐριδήσασθαι</span>
			<i>compete in</i> the foot-race, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.792
			</span></i>.—
				Ep.
			 word : also c. acc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεθυμωμένον
				ἄνδρα μὴ ἐριδαίνειν</span> (fort. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-δμαίνειν</span>) Demetr.Byz. ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				10.452d
			</span></i> ; <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Pisc.</u>
				6
			</span></i> may be a reminiscence of <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.89
			</span></i>.</div>
